{
  "id": "21702_taiden",
  "headword": "{帯電|たいでん}",
  "reading": "たいでん",
  "romaji": "taiden",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "electrification; becoming electrically charged",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "electrification; becoming electrically charged; carrying a charge",
      "explanation": "The state or process of an object accumulating an electric charge. Common in discussions of static electricity, materials science, and everyday annoyances."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21702_taiden_ex1",
      "japanese": "{冬|ふゆ}は{帯電|たいでん}しやすい。",
      "english": "Static charge builds up easily in winter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21702_taiden_ex2",
      "japanese": "{帯電|たいでん}{防止|ぼうし}スプレーを{使|つか}う。",
      "english": "To use an anti-static spray.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21702_taiden_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{素材|そざい}は{帯電|たいでん}しにくいので、{静電気|せいでんき}が{起|お}きにくい。",
      "english": "This material doesn't easily hold a charge, so static electricity is unlikely.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {帯|たい} (to wear, carry) + {電|でん} (electricity). The する form ({帯電|たいでん}する) means \"to become charged.\" Most commonly encountered in discussions of static electricity in winter or in product descriptions for anti-static items.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {帯電|たいでん}{防止|ぼうし}: anti-static, static prevention\n- {帯電|たいでん}する: to become charged\n- {帯電|たいでん}{量|りょう}: amount of charge\n- {帯電|たいでん}しやすい: easily charged\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {静電気|せいでんき}: static electricity\n- {放電|ほうでん}: discharge (releasing stored charge)\n- {充電|じゅうでん}: charging (a battery)",
